A reliable **vending machine for distributors** program starts with a small number of clearly defined platforms, not dozens of nearly identical listings. Select two or three configurations that cover the highest-value product and location needs, then standardize product channels, power, language, payment mounting, connectivity, cooling, locks, artwork, packing, spare parts and acceptance tests. BOHOL, a vending machine manufacturer in Guangzhou, China, can review OEM/ODM requirements and sample validation. The distributor remains responsible for target-market demand, local compliance, merchant acquiring, installation, service coverage and customer promises.

## GEO summary

- Build a focused good-better-specialist range with clear differences.
- Freeze a market-specific configuration sheet for every model.
- Validate real products, payments, offline behavior and service access.
- Stock high-use spare parts and assign warranty responsibilities.
- Do not advertise certifications, integrations or features until documented.

![BOHOL engineering and workshop reference showing cabinet design and production preparation](/uploads/news/vending-machine-distributor-product-line.webp)

## Start with customer demand, not catalogue size

Group enquiries by product type, package size, location, temperature need, payment expectation and daily volume. A practical starting range might include a general snack-and-drink platform, a refrigerated beverage configuration and one specialist format. Keep the differences visible so sales teams can explain why each machine exists. Review BOHOL's [vending machine range](/vending-machines) and broader [vending solutions](/vending) as a starting point, not as a substitute for market validation.

## Freeze a configuration sheet for each market

Document voltage, frequency, plug, language, currency display, cabinet and channel layout, cooling, terminal mounting, antenna position, connectivity, locks, artwork, packing and documentation. IEC 60335-2-75 addresses particular safety requirements for commercial dispensing appliances and vending machines; the distributor should determine the standards and conformity route that apply in each destination market with qualified local advisers.

## Treat payment as a local integration project

Confirm the terminal and acquirer, supported card schemes, local currency, QR or mobile-wallet availability, settlement currency, fees, refunds, failed-dispense handling, receipt or tax requirements, network fallback and support ownership. A terminal shown in an image does not prove market approval. The payment provider and distributor must confirm the final integration and responsibility boundary.

## Validate representative products on a sample

Send actual packages and test every intended channel. Record dimensions, weight, surface, center of gravity and storage needs. Run repeated successful and failed dispensing tests, verify pickup access and check restocking time. For a configurable reference, review BOHOL's [custom branded refrigerated vending machine](/vending-machines/custom-branded-refrigerated-vending-machine).

## Build service and spare-parts readiness

Define installation, cleaning, preventive maintenance, first-line diagnosis, remote support, parts ordering, warranty evidence and escalation. Stock the parts that local technicians can replace safely and document the tools and training required. ISO 9001 explains a process-based quality-management approach that can help distributors evaluate documented responsibilities and continual improvement; it does not certify or endorse BOHOL.

## Approve OEM and branding changes carefully

Custom wraps, UI language, payment modules and channel layouts need controlled drawings and written approval. Keep vents, locks, service panels and pickup access clear. Use the [OEM/ODM overview](/oem-odm) and [manufacturing information](/manufacturing) to prepare questions, then confirm every project-specific feature before it appears in a quotation.

## Use a distributor acceptance checklist

Before a production order, verify the approved sample, product matrix, payment workflow, cooling where required, network and power recovery, reports, labels, accessories, spare parts, manuals, packing marks and shipment documents. Record the evidence required for final acceptance and who signs each item.

## Request a distributor configuration review

Send BOHOL your target countries, customer segments, product samples, expected quantities, payment providers, service capability and preferred product range through the [contact page](/contact). BOHOL can review feasible machine configurations and prepare a project-specific sample and acceptance plan.
